1
00:00:01,550 --> 00:00:04,675
A better public space starts with a difficult conversation.

2
00:00:05,336 --> 00:00:07,062
Everyone has a different priority.

3
00:00:07,726 --> 00:00:09,550
The budget cannot stretch forever.

4
00:00:09,850 --> 00:00:12,637
And a beautiful drawing rarely explains what was left out.

5
00:00:13,296 --> 00:00:14,412
This is Common Ground.

6
00:00:14,798 --> 00:00:17,998
A place for all of us, with an explanation for every tradeoff.

7
00:00:18,877 --> 00:00:20,680
Here is an illustrative pocket park.

8
00:00:21,129 --> 00:00:25,672
We set a budget and minimum commitments to shade, access, play and
water.

9
00:00:26,333 --> 00:00:31,141
The studio checks all four thousand and ninety-six combinations of
twelve interventions.

10
00:00:31,745 --> 00:00:34,418
One hundred and forty-five meet every requirement.

11
00:00:35,126 --> 00:00:38,265
A resident can protect a favorite, like inclusive play.

12
00:00:38,926 --> 00:00:41,330
The entire plan changes around that commitment.

13
00:00:41,858 --> 00:00:43,130
It is still their decision.

14
00:00:43,873 --> 00:00:46,418
Now the budget falls to thirty thousand euros.

15
00:00:47,079 --> 00:00:48,461
There is no feasible plan.

16
00:00:49,255 --> 00:00:53,629
Common Ground does not quietly drop an accessibility target or invent a
result.

17
00:00:54,247 --> 00:00:56,607
It shows the exact requirements that conflict.

18
00:00:57,243 --> 00:00:59,015
Then it asks a more useful question.

19
00:00:59,712 --> 00:01:00,814
What would have to change?

20
00:01:01,356 --> 00:01:05,406
An extra seven thousand euros is enough to satisfy every original
minimum.

21
00:01:06,288 --> 00:01:08,946
That repair is checked against the complete scenario.

22
00:01:09,491 --> 00:01:10,892
We can explore it immediately.

23
00:01:11,550 --> 00:01:15,891
The proposal exports with all its assumptions and a machine-checkable
certificate.

24
00:01:16,654 --> 00:01:20,215
Everything runs in the browser, and the workshop stays on this device.

25
00:01:20,595 --> 00:01:22,574
This is a working design prototype.

26
00:01:23,220 --> 00:01:29,842
Costs and scores are illustrative, and the next step is a facilitated
pilot with residents and local design expertise.

27
00:01:30,439 --> 00:01:32,125
No field impact is claimed.

28
00:01:32,731 --> 00:01:36,943
Common Ground turns a hidden compromise into a conversation people can
actually see.
